            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Natural stone plate, cut, at regional storage</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="c8cad9b0-1ea3-35b8-8ed7-3f876ce5197a">construction</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="28ab7220-acd5-3fbe-9cab-a953ee91777b">others</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The drilling for the mining process is assumed to be done with compressed air, which is produced with electricity. The sawing is assumed to be accomplished with diamond wires. The diamond losses are not taken into account even though they might be significant as no data on diamond production is available. The dust emissions are estimated based on the losses (volume of granite with a density of 2?750 kg/m3) by cutting a plate with the geometry 0.5 * 0.5 * 0.03 m and a weight of 20 kg. It is assumed that 95% of the dust is bound in the cooling water.;
UUID: fa69ed43-cfc5-31f6-b8e8-76d63a6d5bd8</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
